    <!-- ── Help page ── -->
    <string name="help_guide_title">Getting started</string>
    <string name="help_guide_1">Tap \"Install environment\" on the home screen to set up Debian; then tap \"Install\" on any agent you want.</string>
    <string name="help_guide_2">Sign in inside each agent (it keeps its own credentials), and it is ready to use.</string>
    <string name="help_guide_3">Open the \"Terminal\" tab and type an agent command (claude / hermes / agy). OpenCode is built into \"Taiji\" and works out of the box. A separate opencode you install in the terminal is a different copy — the two do not interfere.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_title">Common questions</string>
    <string name="help_faq_q1">Environment won\'t open / download fails?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_a1">Use \"Repair environment\" above to unpack it again — your logins are kept.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_q2">How do I update an agent?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_a2">Re-run the install command in the terminal. To update the system, use \"Check for updates\".</string>
    <string name="help_faq_q3">Where are my files?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_a3">Output goes into the workspace folder (by default Download/证道 on your phone).</string>
    <string name="help_log_location">Location: %1$s</string>
    <string name="help_log_desc">zhengdao-log.txt is this run; timestamped archives keep at most 20 files / 20 MB, oldest deleted first (a clean run is never deleted); errors.log records error lines only. Open them with a file manager, or send them to us to look into a problem.</string>
    <string name="help_log_archive_count">%1$d archived logs.</string>
    <string name="help_log_prev_error">The last run hit an error; the log was kept (copy it and send it to us).</string>
