    <!-- ── Keep-alive page ── -->
    <string name="keepalive_title">Keep-alive</string>
    <string name="keepalive_guide_title">Honor / MagicOS keep-alive guide</string>
    <string name="keepalive_guide_steps">① App launch: Settings → Apps → App launch → Zhengdao → turn off \"Auto-manage\", then allow auto-start / linked start / background activity\n② Battery: Settings → Battery → More battery settings → Zhengdao → set to \"Don\'t optimize\"\n③ Task lock: in Recents find the Zhengdao card, swipe down for the lock icon and tap it\n④ If it exits on its own: Developer options → make sure \"Don\'t keep activities\" is off</string>
    <string name="keepalive_note">Honor is fairly lenient with background services: keep the \"Session running\" notification visible and lock the task, and it will stay alive in the background. If the system does kill it, reopening the terminal takes you back to where you left off.</string>
    <string name="keepalive_battery_btn">One tap: set Zhengdao to \"Don\'t optimize\"</string>
